    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Thorny Hide"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A corbayrant's body is covered in jagged spines. Adjacent creatures that hit them with a melee attack, as well as creatures that touch them or hit them with an unarmed attack, take 4d6 piercing damage and are exposed to thorn paralysis."
            },
            "id": "a07c1fa7-ef5b-4964-a875-082e097ce41a",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:07.180006"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Vitriolic Miasma"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(aura)\n\n30 feet. Non-corbayrants take a \u22122 circumstance penalty to saves against poison effects and gain weakness 10 to poison damage while within the aura."
            },
            "id": "3ce0562e-6c0e-4ecf-baac-f104985c111f",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:07.180006"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Corbayrant Venom"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "**Corbayrant Venom**\nDC: 37\nSaving Throw: Fortitude\nMaximum Duration: 6 rounds\n- Stage 1: 8d6 poison damage (1 round)\n- Stage 2: 9d6 poison damage (1 round)\n- Stage 3: 9d6 poison damage and drained 1 (1 round)"
            },
            "id": "3852b8ff-0ffc-47b9-9193-cc61c831eac5",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:07.180006"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Thorn Paralysis"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(incapacitation, poison)\n\nThe corbayrant's spines are covered in a paralyzing toxin that cause verdurous thorns to sprout from their victim's body. When a non-corbayrant creature is exposed, it attempts a DC 37 Fortitude save.\n\n- **Critical Success:** The creature is unaffected.\n- **Success:** The creature sprouts spines like those of the corbayrant. For 1 minute, the creature gains the corbayrant's thorny hide ability.\n\nAllies attempting to aid the victim with touch-range spells and abilities run the risk of becoming infected themselves. At the end of the duration, the spines fall off harmlessly.\n- **Failure:** As success, but the creature is also paralyzed for 1 minute. It can attempt another Fortitude save at the end of each turn to end the paralysis, but not the spines.\n- **Critical Failure:** As failure, but the creature doesn't receive a save at the end of its turn to end the paralysis."
            },
            "id": "6e6f778f-7585-4924-8f35-c2aaf46c8c79",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:07.180006"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
